& [CrossHostQuestion] must choose the identity being tested
  + [equivalent_environment_reproduction] asks whether independent machines with the same declared toolchain and platform inputs produce the same bytes
  + [diverse_environment_reproduction] asks which declared environment differences preserve bytes and must not silently inherit the equivalent-environment acceptance rule
  + [hermetic_recipe_reproduction] asks whether a versioned toolchain dependency and build image recipe can recreate the artifact independently
  = recommendation: begin with equivalent_environment_reproduction before varying one environment identity at a time

& [RequiredHostReceiptDelta] closes environment identities absent from profile 0.1
  + anonymous host role A or B rather than raw machine or user name
  + Windows edition build architecture and filesystem identity relevant to the build
  + exact rustup toolchain rustc Cargo LLVM target and installed target-component identities
  + resolved MSVC linker binary digest version Windows SDK version and CRT selection
  + Git and tar versions used to create and extract the archive
  + exact allowed build-environment variable set with credentials paths and unrelated variables excluded
  + source commit tree archive Cargo.lock and governed reference identities already present in 0.1
  + output artifact contract field and report behavior identities already present in 0.1

& [Coordinator] compares two independently emitted signed receipts
  + source commit tree archive lockfile build controls governed references and artifact bytes must match for equivalent_environment_reproduction
  + host roles must differ while raw hostname username IP and secret-bearing environment values remain absent
  + toolchain and platform identities must either match exactly or be declared experimental variables before execution
  + receipt comparison is deterministic effect-free and yields passed mismatched or incomparable
  + incomparable is required when a missing identity prevents an honest equivalence claim

& [Evox2ExecutionBoundary] requires new authority before effects
  + remote archive transfer temporary extraction compilation and receipt return are write and compute effects on EVO-X2
  + explicit user authority must name the remote workspace cleanup policy and permitted tool installation policy
  + current llama.cpp process model service ports h8 executable reports and deployment ACL remain read-only and unnecessary to the build
  + provider inference is prohibited because reproducibility does not require it
  - never: replace h8 or change service process model ACL firewall package or signing state as part of the comparison

& [AcceptanceDistinctions] prevent claim inflation
  + same artifact bytes across A and B support cross-host reproduction only for the declared environment relation
  + different bytes with equal governed behavior falsify byte reproduction but may preserve functional behavior as a separate observation
  + matching signatures would prove signer action only after a separately protected signing protocol
  + successful remote build does not establish deployment trust package provenance semantic truth or P1 authority

& [DependencyOrder] is explicit
  + first preserve user authorization and remote effect limits as source
  + second run SJS for host receipt profile coordinator comparison cleanup and falsification
  + third inventory both hosts read-only and determine whether equivalent_environment_reproduction is honestly available
  + fourth execute one clean campaign per host without inference or deployment mutation
  + fifth compare receipts locally then preserve proof faults and an ordinary Git anchor

& [SmallestNextQuestion] is whether to authorize a temporary effect-bounded EVO-X2 build campaign for equivalent-environment comparison
